 "note": "Owner 2026-10-23: does a decision-aware (sibling ranking) loss move O_3's decisions? O_3's recipe (2048-1024-256, outcome head, cut 3, the stored 40M trick-3 base: random s321 25.6M, rules s322 6.4M, harvest s313 8M, validation s401) plus 6M EXACT sibling rows (seed 7911: the frontier positions one choice point's cards lead to, driven by O_3 f5766a) generated in each arm with the same seed, so every arm sees identical rows. Arms differ only in pair_weight (the trainer's gap-weighted pairwise ranking loss over the sibling groups, Fix E, docs/m3-hybrid/sibrank.md; scale 100: a 1% gap is a logit of 1, S2's setting) and seed: base_s1/base_s2 (weight 0: the control and the retraining noise), w1_s1/w1_s2 (weight 1), w3_s1 (weight 3). Each arm is golden-checked in the run (2,000 trick-2 decisions x 320 worlds, 1% re-solved) and judged afterwards on the 100,000 held-out exact sibling rows (sib3, seed 7903) with python/tools/o3_pair_score.py: sibling regret first (sensitive), golden loss second. Needs 190+ threads (labels, golden checks), 128+ GB RAM (46M rows = 87 GB), a GPU with 8+ GB and 120+ GB of disk. Baseline to beat: f5766a 0.0068% (95% bound, seat 1 0.0201%), retraining noise up to about 0.0025 points.",
